-- ============================================================================
-- DR3 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Drilling Hydraulics, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: the circulating pressure chain. Four jobs that pull
-- against each other, and the fourth, not breaking the formation, opposing the
-- other three. A mud as four dial readings converted by two constants, and
-- three models fitted to them: the power law and the Bingham plastic reproduce
-- the 600 and 300 rpm readings exactly and miss the low-rate ones by a factor
-- of five and a factor of two respectively, in opposite directions;
-- Herschel-Bulkley uses three readings, reproduces none exactly, and is what
-- the engine uses through a LOCAL power law evaluated at each element's own
-- shear rate. Pressure loss as a friction factor form with 16 over Re in a
-- pipe, 24 over Re in an annulus, a Bourgoyne turbulent correlation and a
-- linear blend over 800 Reynolds numbers between them, because a discontinuity
-- would be unphysical. The bit as the only inertial loss and the only exact
-- square law. And three losses in series whose exponents against flow rate are
-- about 0.75, about 1.72 and exactly 2, which explain every share in the
-- course.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling against its own goldens, and the teaching lab that the
-- panels and this course share is pinned to the same values by
-- hydraulicsLab.test.js. A numeric sweep over the lessons resolved all 200
-- literals carrying seven or more significant figures to an engine-derived
-- value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks reports zero
-- downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all eighteen graded
-- fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

